{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"body":"Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.\n\nInspected: Configured challenge assertions, their relevant definitions and the cited audited paper statements were compared.","content_sha256":"sha256:68f301089e01a5709d2cfc6ad6f5a8df0c2c17513020c5d4be6ebaf3f9dce5be","fingerprint":"sha256:0042e72101d1a1649b5014b99bafc6bd888807992404bfb3ece5f4db667db9e7","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:f58dc50f5ba15e039e1b859c3b217083f9b04a57b7f0ad9ec7160f2a83b92d39","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.InfiniteMatroidCounterexample.partitional_intersection_counterexample"],"explanation":"The first configured theorem constructs countable partitional self-dual matroids with no packing/covering partition and no intersection witness. HasIntersection encodes a common independent set partitioned into two pieces whose respective closures cover the ground set, so its negation is the intersection corollary. The formal theorem also records the uniform local matroid and ray construction, additional data not contained in this corollary.","fingerprint":"sha256:5e3dd4a9548119e7f1e902e37ddc44ebe7c31b12cf318fbf8e7ff20447a5ed44","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026#cor:intersection","statement_sha256":"sha256:6a1b32006d89ea0453bffa44821d937a986151eb8f47ae786d056e1d33e1cbc4"},{"declarations":["OAI.InfiniteMatroidCounterexample.separate_covering_packing_counterexamples"],"explanation":"The second configured theorem gives a two-member family violating CoveringConjectureFor and a two-member family violating PackingConjectureFor. Those predicates use restrictions for covering and contractions onto the tested subset for packing. This is the separate Covering and Packing Conjectures counterexample corollary.","fingerprint":"sha256:e09491b086a9d2da8391d790ed72b97e4ed2a6b79250a308e56ccca2109464fb","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026#cor:separate-covering-packing","statement_sha256":"sha256:1d9f95d1fb1eccce9cb661c02457cce44fd9d3092bdb63a05abcb423122fe725"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/InfiniteMatroidCorollaries.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L103","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/07-consequences.tex#L32"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:InfiniteMatroidCorollaries","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.InfiniteMatroidCounterexample.partitional_intersection_counterexample","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/InfiniteMatroidCorollaries.lean","line":108,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"f58dc50f5ba15e039e1b859c3b217083f9b04a57b7f0ad9ec7160f2a83b92d39","statement_sha256":"sha256:595e29847d896c777e42dae6f59cc758df17f7cd4382c7214ca505771fce95bf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/InfiniteMatroidCorollaries.lean#L108"},"text":"theorem partitional_intersection_counterexample :\n    Countable E ∧ Infinite E ∧\n    ∃ Q : Matroid E0, Q.E = univ ∧ Q.dual = Q ∧ IsUniform Q ∧\n      let M₀ := rayMatroid Q false\n      let M₁ := rayMatroid Q true\n      M₀.E = univ ∧ M₁.E = univ ∧ M₀.dual = M₀ ∧ M₁.dual = M₁ ∧\n      IsPartitional M₀ ∧ IsPartitional M₁ ∧\n      (∀ I₀ I₁ : Set E, M₀.Indep I₀ → M₁.Indep I₁ → I₀ ∪ I₁ ≠ univ) ∧\n      ¬ HasPackingCovering M₀ M₁ ∧ ¬ HasIntersection M₀ M₁"},{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/1"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/addac8c0237c8061fee48d3e.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.InfiniteMatroidCounterexample.separate_covering_packing_counterexamples","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/InfiniteMatroidCorollaries.lean","line":119,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"f58dc50f5ba15e039e1b859c3b217083f9b04a57b7f0ad9ec7160f2a83b92d39","statement_sha256":"sha256:f697ac77a882847b23b7